<http://data.silknow.org/object/51e1c3a7-a57e-3554-8abe-90d9ad125ea1>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "Jennifer Wearden  'A Torah Ark Curtain: Important Symbolism in a Jewish Hanging' in \"The World of Embroidery\", volume 48, number 5, September 1997, pp. 264-265.\nJennifer Wearden  'Beauty Enhances Ritual: two Italian 17th century embroidered synagogue textiles' in \"Proceedings of The Textile Society of America 1996 Symposium\" 1997 pp. 156-164.\nJewish Ritual Art in the Victoria and Albert Museum by Michael E Keen [London, HMSO, 1991 pp 26-27]\nS Cohen 'A 17th century parochet' in \"The Jewish Chronicle\" 10 July 1953\nKathryn Salomon \"Jewish Ceremonial Art\" [London, Batsford, 1988 fig. 52 p. 73]\nSusan Nashman Fraiman, \"Beyond the Parochet, Three Italian Torah Ark Curtains, Their Makers and Their Meaning\", Master's Thesis, The Hebrew University of Jerusalem, 1998.\nBaker, Malcolm, and Brenda Richardson (eds.), <i>A Grand Design: The Art of the Victoria and Albert Museum</i>, London: V&A Publications, 1999.\n<i>Imagining the Divine. Art and the Rise of World Religions</i>, (eds) Jas Elsner, Stefanie Lenk et al., Ashmolean Museum, University of Oxford, 2017, pp. 12-13\nJoanna Norman, Religious Splendour, in: <i>Princely Treasures: European Masterpieces 1600-1800 from the Victoria and Albert Museum</i>, Sarah Medlam - Lesley Ellis Miller (eds), London 2011, 102-103\n<i>Tutti i colori dell'Italia ebraica. Tessuti preziosi dal tempio di Gerusalemme al prêt-à-porter</i>, eds. Dora Liscia Bemporad and Olga Melasecchi, exhibition catalogue, Florence, Gallerie degli Uffizi, 2019, p. 155 [cat. 24]\n4/35\nNachama, Andreas & Sievernich, Gereon (eds.), <i>Jüdische Lebenswelten, Katalog</i>, Berlin : Berliner Festspiele : Jüdischer Verlag : Suhrkamp Verlag, 1991"@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/50eff59c-c102-3418-bbe3-61071ea8589b> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Jennifer Wearden  'A Torah Ark Curtain: Important Symbolism in a Jewish Hanging' in \"The World of Embroidery\", volume 48, number 5, September 1997, pp. 264-265.\nJennifer Wearden  'Beauty Enhances Ritual: two Italian 17th century embroidered synagogue textiles' in \"Proceedings of The Textile Society of America 1996 Symposium\" 1997 pp. 156-164.\nJewish Ritual Art in the Victoria and Albert Museum by Michael E Keen [London, HMSO, 1991 pp 26-27]\nS Cohen 'A 17th century parochet' in \"The Jewish Chronicle\" 10 July 1953\nKathryn Salomon \"Jewish Ceremonial Art\" [London, Batsford, 1988 fig. 52 p. 73]\nSusan Nashman Fraiman, \"Beyond the Parochet, Three Italian Torah Ark Curtains, Their Makers and Their Meaning\", Master's Thesis, The Hebrew University of Jerusalem, 1998.\nBaker, Malcolm, and Brenda Richardson (eds.), <i>A Grand Design: The Art of the Victoria and Albert Museum</i>, London: V&A Publications, 1999.\n<i>Imagining the Divine. Art and the Rise of World Religions</i>, (eds) Jas Elsner, Stefanie Lenk et al., Ashmolean Museum, University of Oxford, 2017, pp. 12-13\nJoanna Norman, Religious Splendour, in: <i>Princely Treasures: European Masterpieces 1600-1800 from the Victoria and Albert Museum</i>, Sarah Medlam - Lesley Ellis Miller (eds), London 2011, 102-103\n<i>Tutti i colori dell'Italia ebraica. Tessuti preziosi dal tempio di Gerusalemme al prêt-à-porter</i>, eds. Dora Liscia Bemporad and Olga Melasecchi, exhibition catalogue, Florence, Gallerie degli Uffizi, 2019, p. 155 [cat. 24]\n4/35\nNachama, Andreas & Sievernich, Gereon (eds.), <i>Jüdische Lebenswelten, Katalog</i>, Berlin : Berliner Festspiele : Jüdischer Verlag : Suhrkamp Verlag, 1991"@en .

